@startuml
left to right direction

actor Student
actor Administrator

rectangle "Smart Campus Study Room Booking System" {

  usecase "UC-01\nView availability" as UC01
  usecase "UC-02\nBook room" as UC02
  usecase "UC-03\nCancel booking" as UC03
  usecase "UC-04\nReceive confirmation" as UC04
  usecase "UC-05\nBlock room" as UC05
  usecase "UC-06\nUnblock room" as UC06
  usecase "UC-07\nReview room usage" as UC07
}

Student --> UC01
Student --> UC02
Student --> UC03

Administrator --> UC05
Administrator --> UC06
Administrator --> UC07

' why: A successful booking includes sending the required confirmation (R4).
UC02 --> UC04 : <<include>>

' why: The approved US-04 requires confirmation after a student cancels a booking.
UC03 --> UC04 : <<include>>

note bottom of UC02
Business rules:
- R1: Booking starts in the future and lasts more than 0 and at most 2 hours.
- R2: Active bookings for the same room cannot overlap.
- R3: A blocked room cannot accept a new booking.
- R4: A successful booking produces a confirmation.
end note

note right of UC04
Confirmation is an outcome of
booking or cancellation.
No actor invokes this use case directly.
end note

note bottom of UC03
Assumption:
Touching bookings such as 10:00–12:00
and 12:00–13:00 do not overlap.
end note

note bottom of UC05
Assumption:
Blocking a room does not cancel or modify
existing bookings.
end note

@enduml
